      "abstract": "Genomic prediction has revolutionized dairy breeding by improving lactation curve precision and accelerating genetic selection cycles. While current recurrent neural networks (RNN) demonstrate adaptability for modeling test-day milk yield (TDMY) sequences, their predictive accuracy remains suboptimal. Our study presents a threefold enhancement framework: 1) A bidirectional LSTM architecture that prevents gradient explosion while capturing bidirectional temporal patterns; 2) Embedded self-attention mechanisms enabling adaptive feature weighting during data preprocessing; 3) Comprehensive ablation studies validating architectural efficacy. By synergistically integrating these innovations, we establish a robust machine learning paradigm that significantly improves phenotypic characterization of continuous lactation patterns for genomic prediction applications.",
