      "abstract": "This paper presents a comprehensive review of a 100-kW-class piston hybrid power system for long-endurance UAVs. The typical system architecture of the hybrid power system is introduced in the first section. This is followed by a discussion of the key technologies of the piston engine, which possesses high efficiency, high power density, and high reliability. At the same time, the high power density generator and electric propulsion technologies are analyzed, including the starter/generator, the cooling structure, the rectifier, and the matching of parameters of each part. A comparative analysis of the three kinds of energy management and control strategies of the hybrid power system is then conducted. Finally, the integration and testing methods of the hybrid power system are discussed. Consequently, it is determined that the hybrid power system, which is characterized by its high efficiency, reliability, and intelligence, is emerging as the predominant approach for enhancing the performance and engineering of next-generation UAV platforms.",
